ll,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-30T05:08:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-30T08:57:09Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7, 4.7.1, 4.8.dev.1, 4.8.dev.2, master\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev2.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9595) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 31.88 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nLoading a WAV file with an odd amount of bytes, using either load_from_file or load_from_buffer causes error spam.\n\nCode:\n```gdscript\nextends AudioStreamPlayer\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tstream = AudioStreamWAV.load_from_file(\"res://WCCK Jingles.wav\")\n```\n\nResults:\n\n<img width=\"380\" height=\"381.5\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ba043f4c-f556-4e34-a65e-7c29112f33f7\" />\n\nEach error is the same and expands to this:\n```c\nE 0:00:00:860   new_script.gd:4 @ _ready(): Condition \"p_position > length\" is true.\n  <C++ Source>  core/io/file_access_memory.cpp:101 @ seek()\n  <Stack Trace> new_script.gd:4 @ _ready()\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Import and open the MRP project.\n2. Run the project.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[wav-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30531770/wav-mrp.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121918/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godote